  "representation": "Relaxed binary row-domain CSP. For each A vertex, the cross-neighbour row has size 10-deg_A through 12-deg_A. Each row is triangle-free in B; for an A-edge the two-row intersection is independent in B; for an A-nonedge the two-row union hits every independent 4-set of B. B-column degrees, global degree-class counts, total cross-edge count, and all constraints involving 3 or more A rows are deliberately omitted. Therefore this is a strict superfamily of the real gluing problem, and UNSAT is a rigorous exclusion.",
